WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:06.290
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and hopefully
by now you’ve seen the Deadpool comic con

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:07.290
trailer.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:12.309
What happened was a high def version of test
footage was leaked by the people that made

00:00:12.309 --> 00:00:13.309
the footage.

00:00:13.309 --> 00:00:15.741
Fox commissioned them to do a test for a Deadpool
movie back in 2011.

00:00:15.741 --> 00:00:20.290
So that footage was what you were watching
if you saw it.

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:22.510
This video is going to be a breakdown of what
that whole thing was about and what’s going

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:23.510
on with the Deadpool movie right now.

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:29.920
A couple of big people close to the project
are doing a fun experiment.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:38.109
In case you’re just finding me for the first
time I do Marvel and DC videos every week.

00:00:38.109 --> 00:00:40.010
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.579
So starting with the leaked footage.

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:42.839
Here’s the real story:

00:00:42.839 --> 00:00:45.340
Blur Studios is the effects house that made
the trailer.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:48.010
They are the ones that posted it the week
before comic con.

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:51.379
It was done without Fox’s knowledge, Fox
had nothing to do with it and right after

00:00:51.379 --> 00:00:53.329
it posted the video was taken down.

00:00:53.329 --> 00:00:56.780
Then people reuploaded it and it got taken
down again, rinse and repeat.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.160
The trailer wasn’t part of a Fox Panel or
anything.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:08.590
It was just the people behind the film trying
to get Fox to see that there was demand for

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:09.590
it.

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:14.440
Even though the Test Footage is from 2011,
FOX still hasn’t given the movie a greenlight.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.800
The trailer itself features Ryan Reynolds
voicing the character and presumably he’s

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.450
still down to play the role if the movie ever
happens.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:23.610
Here’s some background on where the movie
is:

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:24.890
There is a finished script.

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:27.310
It was written by Rhett Reese and Paul Wernick.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:31.210
Ryan Reynolds along with all the other people
who have read it say it’s great.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:35.840
Up at the top, Lauren Schuler Donner and fellow
producer Simon Kinberg are open to the idea

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:40.420
of a Deadpool movie but the belief is that
other people at Fox are hesitant to make an

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:41.910
R-Rated Comic Book movie.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:45.140
I feel like we can all agree that a Deadpool
movie would have to be a hard-R in order to

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:46.140
be taken seriously.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:49.520
The source material isn’t like anything
we’ve seen recently and that’s part of

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:51.930
the reason why we haven’t heard anything
new about the movie.

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:56.800
For example, Guardians of the Galaxy is a
movie about a bunch of assholes being ridiculous

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:57.800
and funny and violent.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:01.450
But Deadpool is a cold-blooded killer, it’s
in the name.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:04.900
His body count would be higher than a zombie
apocalypse movie.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:09.090
Right now, the comic book movie culture is
tuned for family friendly stories.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:18.030
The closest example of a hard R marvel film
is the last Punisher film, War Zone.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:22.569
Any time you walk into an office at FOX and
ask for 70 Million dollars to make an R-Rated

00:02:22.569 --> 00:02:26.719
comic book movie, all they have to do is point
at Punisher and say “it’s not going to

00:02:26.719 --> 00:02:27.719
work”.

00:02:27.719 --> 00:02:30.439
Nobody wants to make a movie that isn’t
guaranteed to earn a billion dollars.

00:02:30.439 --> 00:02:34.379
How do you make a Deadpool movie that earns
a billion dollars?

00:02:34.379 --> 00:02:35.379
There are a couple of options.

00:02:35.379 --> 00:02:39.319
Mostly, you tune it down to PG 13 so you can
market it to a bigger audience.

00:02:39.319 --> 00:02:43.819
Also, foreign markets like China have very
strict rules about violence in films.

00:02:43.819 --> 00:02:47.190
If you can get a movie released in China,
that’s an extra 100 million dollars you

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:48.280
could potentially make.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:54.550
That’s why Transformers put so many Chinese
things in their movie.

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:56.819
So the Chinese government would release it.

00:02:56.819 --> 00:03:00.110
The government controls which movies get released
there.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:03.530
It’s crazy I know.

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:06.349
But all most studios care about is making
money.

00:03:06.349 --> 00:03:13.349
Which is where we get to the creators and
the Deadpool Experiment that’s happening

00:03:13.349 --> 00:03:14.349
right now.

00:03:14.349 --> 00:03:18.250
Right now on twitter Rhett Reese, the guy
who wrote the script started an experiment

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:24.430
to see who would buy a ticket for an R-Rated
Deadpool movie.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:27.599
Even Rob Liefeld, the artist on the Deadpool
comic book jumped on board.

00:03:27.599 --> 00:03:31.610
It just started but I’ll post a link in
the description if you guys want to participate.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:38.319
He’s just asking you to retweet his tweet
as a way to show FOX people really are interested

00:03:38.319 --> 00:03:40.519
in a Deadpool movie.

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:44.019
I know a lot of you guys are asking why don’t
they just do a Kickstarter?

00:03:44.019 --> 00:03:46.049
If fans want it bad enough, they’ll fund
it themselves.

00:03:46.049 --> 00:03:50.629
The reason they can’t do that is FOX owns
the rights, so the only way the filmmakers

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:53.840
could kickstart a Deadpool movie would be
if FOX said okay.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:55.769
And they haven’t, so no kickstarter.

00:03:55.769 --> 00:04:00.969
I haven’t read the script, but here are
my top picks for stories I think they should

00:04:00.969 --> 00:04:01.969
do:

00:04:01.969 --> 00:04:03.909
At the top is Joe Kelley’s run.

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:07.489
It’s collected in an omnibus if you guys
haven’t read it yet, his run started in

00:04:07.489 --> 00:04:08.489
1997.

00:04:08.489 --> 00:04:12.120
He’s the one that gave Deadpool all the
signature character traits you see in the

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:13.419
current comics.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:17.590
Start to finish it was one of the best collections
of Deadpool stories ever.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:23.110
Most of the Deadpool pictures you see people
posting come from this run.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:24.919
After that there’s Deadpool’s time on
X-Force.

00:04:24.919 --> 00:04:27.599
It’s Rick Remender’s run on Uncanny X-Force.

00:04:27.599 --> 00:04:30.630
It’s collected in an omnibus too in case
you guys want to read it all.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:35.091
It started in 2010 with Uncanny X-Force Number
1 and went to issue 35.

00:04:35.091 --> 00:04:41.830
There is an X-Force movie in development at
Fox, so even if they don’t give Deadpool

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:45.379
a solo movie, they could make him a member
of X-Force or at least a part of the movie

00:04:45.379 --> 00:04:49.729
if he’s not a part of the team.

00:04:49.729 --> 00:04:53.710
Usually when people make new team-based comic
book movies they keep it really simple.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:56.370
Like X-Men started with a small cast and then
expanded.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:05:00.039
So I’m not expecting Fox to jam Deadpool
into their first X-Force movie.

00:05:00.039 --> 00:05:04.930
But he could cameo like he did in Wolverine
Origins.

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:08.330
After those two runs, I think Merc With A
Mouth would make for a great movie.

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:11.280
That was Deadpool in the Savage Land.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:14.930
Picture him walking around with his decaying
severed head that he talks too.

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:18.030
That might be a little much to expect from
a movie, but I’d love to see them include

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:19.580
the talking head as an easter egg.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:23.960
They kind of did that in the Wolverine Origins
movie but it’s not about him just talking

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:24.960
to a severed head.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:27.870
The head has to look like he’s been carrying
it around all year.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:29.599
Super gross but not quite a skeleton.

00:05:29.599 --> 00:05:35.880
Let me know if you guys would rather see Ryan
Reynolds come back or if you want to see someone

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:36.880
new.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:40.349
His career has kind of hit a speedbump recently
so this seems like the kind of project he

00:05:40.349 --> 00:05:42.879
would jump on just because it’s high profile.

00:05:42.879 --> 00:05:50.820
I’d really like to see somebody new come
in.

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:55.500
Zachary Quinto did a great job of playing
a crazy supervillain on Heroes even if that

00:05:55.500 --> 00:06:00.030
show lost some steam, Jonathan Rhys-Meyers
is another person who’s great at playing

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:01.030
crazy people.

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:06.879
I don’t picture deadpool with a british
accent and if you saw Dracula Season 1, I

00:06:06.879 --> 00:06:08.750
hated his fake american accent.

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:11.150
But he’s another strong choice.

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:14.720
If Jeremy Renner weren’t already Hawkeye
I would add him to my Deadpool list.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:18.250
Interesting side note: there was actually
an awesome Deadpool vs Hawkeye storyline in

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:20.290
the comics during Dark Reign.

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:26.810
Sam Worthington would have to go a little
over the top but he has the right physique

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:27.840
for it.

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:30.159
And I could maybe get on board with Tom Hardy.

00:06:30.159 --> 00:06:32.439
I’m looking forward to seeing him in Mad
Max fury road.

00:06:32.439 --> 00:06:36.630
I think he’d have a harder time selling
the comedic aspects of Deadpool, but I think

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:37.630
he could do it.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:41.750
But let me know which other actors you think
would make good Deadpool’s.

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:46.060
As of right now I don’t think we’ll see
an actual Deadpool movie until after X-Force.

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:49.360
And that movie won’t get here till well
after X-Men Apocalypse.

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:55.069
They are working on a new Old Man Logan Wolverine
solo movie for Hugh Jackman so expect that

00:06:55.069 --> 00:06:56.319
to come before Deadpool too.

00:06:56.319 --> 00:07:00.889
I think those movies are the real reason FOX
isn’t rushing into Deadpool.

00:07:00.889 --> 00:07:03.750
They feel like they have the X-Men and Wolverine
movie formula down.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:15.759
They can make those movies and guarantee a
big profit.

00:07:15.759 --> 00:07:23.759
So they don’t have to scramble for new franchises.

00:07:23.759 --> 00:07:29.250
So in related news, Since all of you guys
voted for it I’ll be doing new Doctor Who

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:30.290
and Legend of Korra next.

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:33.960
I’ll try to have all of that stuff up by
Saturday morning but you can follow me on

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:35.840
twitter and facebook for updates.

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:37.540
Links to all that at the bottom of the description.

